          "dense_rank": 1,
          "lexical_score": 9.79574,
          "lexical_rank": 1,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Seasonal flu vaccine\n\nWe give the flu vaccine every year from the start of September until the end of March. Patients aged 65 and over are offered a high-dose vaccine (Fluzone High-Dose), which gives a stronger immune response at that age. The flu vaccine can be given at the same appointment as a COVID-19 vaccine.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.45642042,
          "dense_rank": 2,
          "lexical_score": 4.3375964,
          "lexical_rank": 6,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## COVID-19 vaccine\n\nWe offer the updated COVID-19 vaccine for the current season made by Pfizer-BioNTech (Comirnaty). We do not stock the Moderna (Spikevax) or Novavax vaccines.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.45515087,
          "dense_rank": 3,
          "lexical_score": 3.4496043,
          "lexical_rank": 8,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Tetanus, diphtheria and whooping cough (Tdap)\n\nAdults need a tetanus booster every 10 years. We use Boostrix, which also protects against diphtheria and whooping cough (pertussis).",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.44444907,
          "dense_rank": 4,
          "lexical_score": 4.3133082,
          "lexical_rank": 7,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## After your vaccination\n\nPlease stay in the waiting area for 15 minutes after any vaccination, so staff can help if you feel faint or have an allergic reaction. A sore arm for a day or two is common. Bring your vaccination record to the appointment so the new dose can be added to it.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.42167225,
          "dense_rank": 5,
          "lexical_score": 4.4073224,
          "lexical_rank": 5,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Travel vaccinations\n\nBook a travel vaccination appointment at least six weeks before you leave, because some vaccines need more than one dose or take time to become effective. Bring your travel dates and the list of countries you are visiting. We offer:\n\n- hepatitis A (Havrix): two doses six to twelve months apart, and one dose before travel protects you for the trip;\n- typhoid, either as an injection (Typhim Vi) given at least two weeks before travel, or as an oral vaccine (Vivotif) of four capsules taken on alternate days and finished at least one week before travel;\n- hepatitis B (Engerix-B): three doses over six months.\n\nWe do not offer the yellow fever vaccine, which can only be given at a registered yellow fever vaccination centre. We also do not offer rabies or Japanese encephalitis vaccines.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.37901953,
          "dense_rank": 6,
          "lexical_score": 4.407723,
          "lexical_rank": 4,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Self-pay vaccine prices\n\nIf your insurance does not cover a vaccine, these are the self-pay prices: flu vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, ty",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 37,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.35104486,
          "dense_rank": 7,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Minor procedures\n\nWe freeze common warts and verrucas with cryotherapy (liquid nitrogen). A wart may need two to four treatments, about three weeks apart. We do not remo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 22,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3022247,
          "dense_rank": 8,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 24,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3011737,
          "dense_rank": 9,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 37,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2839867,
          "dense_rank": 10,
          "lexical_score": 3.2344062,
          "lexical_rank": 9,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 23,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2817217,
          "dense_rank": 11,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2813968,
          "dense_rank": 12,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 34,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.27296495,
          "dense_rank": 13,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Email\n\nWe use email only to confirm a new appointment and to send an itemized receipt you have asked for. We do not send test results or medical",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 20,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27117157,
          "dense_rank": 14,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.2700281,
          "dense_rank": 15,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Cigna\n\nWe are in-network with Cigna Open Access Plus (OAP) and Cigna PPO plans. Cigna LocalPlus plans are in-network only for members who live in our county; the network area",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 31,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2697363,
          "dense_rank": 16,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.2651953,
          "dense_rank": 17,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## UnitedHealthcare\n\nWe are in-network with UnitedHealthcare Choice Plus and UnitedHealthcare Options PPO. UnitedHealthcare Navigate HMO is not in-network. AARP Medicare Advanta",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 37,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.26305622,
          "dense_rank": 18,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medical examinations, pilot medicals or immigration medical examinations. A",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.25554726,
          "dense_rank": 19,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medicare (Part B) for medical visits. Medicare does not cover routine dental care, so dental appointments are self-pay for Medicare ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 36,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2498931,
          "dense_rank": 20,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Who can see your medical record\n\nYour record can be seen only by the practitioners and staff involved in your care at the clinic, and by the staff who han",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 35,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.24754389,
          "dense_rank": 21,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact an",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.2473456,
          "dense_rank": 22,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Blue Cross Blue Shield\n\nWe are in-network with Blue Cross Blue Shield PPO plans, including BlueCard PPO members whose plan was issued in another state; look for the suitcase ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.24648045,
          "dense_rank": 23,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Aetna\n\nWe are in-network with Aetna Choice POS II and Aetna Open Access Managed Choice. Aetna Medicare Advantage PPO plans are in-network as well. Plans administered by Aetna",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.24426982,
          "dense_rank": 24,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 30,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.24256638,
          "dense_rank": 25,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Dental insurance\n\nMedical insurance plans do not cover dental care. For dental appointments we accept these dental plans: Delta Dental PPO, MetLife PDP Plus and Guardian DentalG",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": null,
          "dense_rank": null,
          "lexical_score": 4.559439,
          "lexical_rank": 2,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If your plan has a deductible you have not met yet, you pay the amount your plan allows for the visit at check-in. The front desk can estimate that amount for you if you give them your plan details before the visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 7,
          "similarity_score": null,
          "dense_rank": null,
          "lexical_score": 4.4712873,
          "lexical_rank": 3,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Updating your insurance\n\nIf your insurance has changed since your last visit, tell the front desk at check-in and fill in Form IC-2, the Insurance Update Form, so the claim goes to the right plan. A new card can take up to two business days to verify. If you give us the new details at least two business days before your appointment, we can confirm your coverage before you arrive.",
          "text_truncated": false
